ai.agent-kinds | keys: param | global: keyed by the project endpoint and agent name: the kind the project's listing reported, the same for every caller of the project; it only decides the workflow opt-in header | replica-local: filled by this replica's project listings; another replica learns the kind from its own listing (24 h TTL)
ai.context-windows | keys: tenant, param, param, param | tenant | replica-local: context windows learned from a provider's rejection; another replica pays one rejected call and learns it too (24 h TTL)
ai.embed-dims-refusals | keys: param | global: keyed by the embeddings endpoint and model: a model that refuses `dimensions` refuses it for every caller | replica-local: learned from an upstream rejection; another replica pays the one rejection round trip and learns it too (24 h TTL)
ai.param-repairs | keys: param | global: keyed by the upstream endpoint and model: a parameter the deployment refuses is a fact about the deployment, the same for every caller; it only shapes the next request | replica-local: learned from an upstream rejection; another replica pays the one rejection round trip and learns it too (1 h TTL)
ai.responses-tool-routes | keys: param | global: keyed by the resource's Responses route and deployment: whether the route serves the deployment is the same for every caller | replica-local: learned from the upstream's answer; another replica pays the one refused or rerouted round trip and learns it too (1 h TTL)
ai.served-by-resource | keys: param, param, param | global: keyed by resource and deployment: a deployment serves the same model for every caller of its resource; the answer only shapes the request (the Claude route), never a model list | replica-local: the resource-wide view of ai.served-models, learned from responses; another replica relearns it from its next answer (24 h TTL)
ai.served-models | keys: tenant, param, param, param | tenant | replica-local: alias to served model, learned from responses; another replica relearns it from its next answer (24 h TTL)
ai.stream-refusals | keys: param | global: keyed by the upstream endpoint and deployment: a model that refuses streaming refuses it for every caller | replica-local: learned from an upstream rejection; another replica pays the one rejection round trip and learns it too (1 h TTL)
analysis.shared-runs | keys: tenant, resource, content | tenant | replica-local: decoded copies of the runs the shared report pair (analysis.pair) stores, keyed by the run's identity, so a copy never goes stale; another replica decodes its own on a miss
analyzer.reports | keys: tenant, resource, version, rule-profile, content | tenant | replica-local: a function of the document, rule profile and analyzer version; another replica recomputes on a miss, and the desktop session analytics it backs live in one process
analyzer.suppression-inventory | keys: tenant, version, rule-profile, content | tenant | replica-local: a function of the document, rule profile and analyzer version; another replica recomputes on a miss
azure.owner-memos | keys: tenant, param | tenant | replica-local: a 60 s memo of a durable marker and two rate limits; another replica reads the marker and keeps its own limits
chat.context | keys: tenant, resource, version, param, param, param, param, param, param, param, param, param | tenant | replica-local: a turn is served by the replica its stream runs on; another rebuilds the context on a miss
chat.history-scrubs | keys: tenant, content | tenant | replica-local: a pure function of the caller's text; another replica scrubs it again
chat.scrubbed-docs | keys: tenant, resource, version | tenant | replica-local: a turn is served by the replica its stream runs on; another re-scrubs the flow on a miss
chat.token-counts | keys: param, content | global: a token count is a function of the provider's tokenizer and the text alone, shared across users like the system prompts it mostly counts | replica-local: a pure function of the text; another replica counts it again
dashboard.analytics | keys: tenant, param, param | tenant | shared: redis-inval: a flow change or analysis on any replica drops the views of the owner and of the flow's org on every replica once committed; the 30 s TTL bounds a lost message and other collaborators' views
dashboard.home | keys: tenant, version | tenant | shared: redis-inval: a flow change or analysis on any replica drops the owner's view on every replica once committed; the 30 s TTL bounds a lost message and other collaborators' views
flow.ast | keys: tenant, param, content | tenant | replica-local: desktop and local mode only (no storage backend): parsed from bytes the caller holds, re-parsed on a miss
flow.documents | keys: resource | global: flow ids are globally unique; every read re-checks the header under the caller's RLS and serves the entry only at the stored version | replica-local: validated against the stored version on every read: another replica's write is seen at once
flow.search-index | keys: resource | global: served only for the exact document object it was built from, which the caller resolved through an authorized read | replica-local: rebuilt from the document on a miss
flow.upload-ids | keys: tenant, content | tenant | replica-local: the local half of the memo: with Redis configured the id is also claimed under the flow.upload-id key, which every replica reads first, so a miss here costs a lookup; without it a miss mints a new flow id and an identical re-upload through another replica creates a second flow, as after the TTL
providers.model-listings | keys: tenant, param | tenant | shared: redis-inval: a credential change on any replica drops the listings on every replica once committed; the 10 min TTL bounds a lost message
rag.corpus-counts | keys: tenant | tenant | shared: redis-inval: an upload, delete or re-index on any replica drops the count on every replica once committed; the 30 s TTL bounds a lost message
rag.embedders | keys: tenant, version | tenant | shared: redis-inval: a credential, provider-policy, settings or membership change on any replica drops the caller's or the organisation's memo on every replica once committed; the 60 s TTL bounds a lost message and a registry designation change
rag.identity-census | keys: tenant, param, version | tenant | replica-local: keyed by the org's corpus generation, which an upload, delete or re-index on any replica moves through rag.corpus-counts; the 30 s TTL bounds a lost message
rag.query-embeddings | keys: tenant, param, content | tenant | replica-local: 10 min TTL; a function of the embedder and the query, recomputed on a miss
rag.stranded-docs | keys: tenant, param, version | tenant | replica-local: keyed by the org's corpus generation, which an upload, delete or re-index on any replica moves through rag.corpus-counts; the 30 s TTL bounds a lost message
rules.deployment-profile | keys: none | global: the deployment layer alone (no org): deployment settings and the operator's rule file, the same for every reader | shared: redis-inval: a deployment settings change on any replica drops it on every replica once committed; the 30 s TTL bounds a lost message
rules.profiles | keys: tenant | tenant | shared: redis-inval: a rule or membership change on any replica drops it on every replica once committed; the 30 s TTL bounds a lost message
settings.deployment | keys: none | global: one deployment-wide settings row, the same for every caller | shared: redis-inval: a write on any replica drops it on every replica once committed; the 30 s TTL bounds a lost message
